Batch manager:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This command allows you to list the files currently selected for batch download. The list shows the file name, size, approx. download time, wether the file is on the HD and wether it is free.

At each screenfull you are given a prompt. From here you may continue, quit, delete files, remove all, or get info.

Quit: This command will stop printing any more tagged files. The program will display your totals and exit.

Delete: You may delete files ranging from 1 to the total number of tagged files. Its better if you only delete files listed on the screen. Numeric input can be single numbers, a range of numbers (1-5 NO SPACES), or a combination.

   *** Only numbers may be used for file deletion ***

Remove all: This will delete your tagged list. It exists for quick deletetion, and to delete the file should it become corrupt somehow.

Info: This command will display the totals so far.

At the end of the program, you are shown your old totals, and your new totals. These lines will be the same if you haven't deleted any files from your list.

%RETURN
